<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abu'l-Fazl Bayhaqi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">995–1077</span> · Also known as Abolfazl Beyhaqi, Abu'l-Fadl Bayhaqi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abu'l-Fazl Bayhaqi was a Persian secretary in the chancery of the Ghaznavid sultans and a historian. His multi-volume history of the dynasty, of which the part on the reign of Mas'ud I survives as the Tarikh-i Bayhaqi, describes court life, politics and personalities in vivid detail, using documents and his own observation. It is regarded as a masterpiece of early Persian prose.</p></div>
